1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,865
周一早上
It's Monday morning.

2
00:00:01,915 --> 00:00:06,394
一个将近三百五十行的文件，八十三个 notebook
There's a file of almost three hundred and fifty lines, eighty-three notebooks,

3
00:00:06,394 --> 00:00:08,379
还有从二月一路积累下来的结果
and results going back to February.

4
00:00:08,699 --> 00:00:10,366
接下来这一个小时，该花在哪里？
Where does the next hour go?

5
00:00:10,416 --> 00:00:13,472
Josh 不是靠先把一切都规划好来回答这个问题的
Josh doesn't answer that by planning everything first.

6
00:00:13,792 --> 00:00:18,144
他运行代码，读第一个坏掉的地方，只修那一处
He runs the code, reads the first thing that breaks, and fixes only that.

7
00:00:18,464 --> 00:00:20,960
这一集把这个习惯变成一套方法
This episode turns that habit into a method.

8
00:00:23,233 --> 00:00:24,867
先看能用的部分
Start with what works.

9
00:00:24,867 --> 00:00:27,021
只用 identity 模型的话
With only the identity model,

10
00:00:27,021 --> 00:00:30,290
整条流水线在玩具数据上已经能跑通
the whole pipeline already runs on toy data:

11
00:00:30,290 --> 00:00:33,409
setup、train、predict、evaluate，没有报错
setup, train, predict, evaluate. No errors.

12
00:00:33,566 --> 00:00:38,942
这叫「会走路的骨架」：每个阶段都已经从头到尾存在，哪怕大多还很单薄
That's a walking skeleton: every stage exists, end to end, even though most are thin.

13
00:00:39,262 --> 00:00:43,486
从这里开始，你一次加粗一根骨头，骨架始终能走
From here, you thicken one bone at a time, and the skeleton keeps walking.

14
00:00:44,066 --> 00:00:46,775
但看看 evaluate 返回了什么：什么也没有
But look at what evaluate returned: nothing.

15
00:00:47,095 --> 00:00:49,058
分数算出来就被丢掉了
The scores were computed and dropped.

16
00:00:49,378 --> 00:00:54,562
所以第一项任务自己冒了出来：把分数作为一张「模型 × 指标」的表返回
So the first task writes itself: return the scores as a table, models by metrics.

17
00:00:56,900 --> 00:00:59,247
现在加上 scGen 继续跑
Now add scGen and keep running.

18
00:00:59,567 --> 00:01:02,276
停下来猜一猜：哪个阶段最先坏？
Pause and predict: which stage breaks first?

19
00:01:06,433 --> 00:01:10,170
我们用玩具数据和一个替身 scgen 把每个阶段都跑了一遍
We ran each stage on toy data, with a stand-in for scgen,

20
00:01:10,170 --> 00:01:13,580
每次只打刚好够走到那一步的最小补丁
patching only the smallest thing needed to reach it.

21
00:01:13,900 --> 00:01:16,887
下面就是这串足迹，按程序遇到它们的顺序排列
Here's the trail, in the order the program reaches it.

22
00:01:17,033 --> 00:01:22,929
setup：AttributeError，x_dimensions，第 253 行——第二集讲过
Setup: an attribute error, x_dimensions, line 253. That was episode two.

23
00:01:22,929 --> 00:01:24,567
train：TypeError
Train: a type error.

24
00:01:24,567 --> 00:01:30,708
train 缺少 training_data 参数，因为第 133 行调用它时什么也没传
Train is missing its training data, because line 133 calls it with nothing.

25
00:01:30,867 --> 00:01:33,310
predict：第 288 行的 NameError
Predict: a name error at line 288,

26
00:01:33,310 --> 00:01:37,694
用到的辅助函数定义在 train 内部，predict 看不见它
a helper that lives inside train, where predict can't see it.

27
00:01:38,014 --> 00:01:42,297
evaluate：真实数据里小鼠和人类细胞数不同
Evaluate: once mouse and human have different cell counts,

28
00:01:42,297 --> 00:01:46,653
R² 就没法把两边的细胞一一配对，第 313 行
as real data do, R squared can't line them up, at line 313.

29
00:01:46,833 --> 00:01:49,605
每个错误就是待办看板上的一张卡片
Each error is one card on your to-do board.

30
00:01:49,605 --> 00:01:52,958
沿着 scGen 这条路，顺序由程序交给你
Along scGen's path, the program hands you the order.

31
00:01:52,958 --> 00:01:55,601
你只需要决定先走哪一条路
You only choose which path to walk first.

32
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:01,407
有些卡片现在还不是报错
Some cards aren't errors yet.

33
00:02:01,407 --> 00:02:06,328
Josh 的 notebook 显示，小鼠训练文件有 18,024 个基因
Josh's notebook shows a mouse training file with about eighteen thousand genes,

34
00:02:06,328 --> 00:02:09,256
人类训练文件有 61,759 个
and a human one with almost sixty-two thousand.

35
00:02:09,256 --> 00:02:11,312
而测试文件只有 1,000 个
The test files hold one thousand.

36
00:02:11,467 --> 00:02:15,222
在它们共享同一个基因轴之前，一个网络没法把它们都读进去
One network can't read them all until they share one gene axis.

37
00:02:15,542 --> 00:02:20,256
对齐基因是数据的工作，所以它应该放在数据类旁边
Lining up genes is a data job, so it belongs next to the data classes.

38
00:02:20,433 --> 00:02:23,708
不过第一次复现时，这一步已经做好了
But for your first replication, it's already done.

39
00:02:23,708 --> 00:02:28,031
M1 第 8 版的文件已有一份共享的一千个基因列表
The M1 version eight file has one shared list of a thousand genes.

40
00:02:28,031 --> 00:02:33,010
它是一张表加一份切分规则，而你的数据类要的是四个文件
It's one table plus a split recipe, while your data classes take four files.

41
00:02:33,010 --> 00:02:38,119
所以真正的卡片是：把这张表切成训练和测试、小鼠和人类四份
So the real card is: split that table into training and test, mouse and human.

42
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:45,424
停一下：八十三个 notebook 里，你会先复现哪一个？ 为什么？
Pause: out of eighty-three notebooks, which would you replicate first, and why?

43
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:50,958
答案不是某个 notebook
Not a notebook.

44
00:02:51,008 --> 00:02:56,116
选你的项目早已称作「冻结基准」的第一个切分
Pick the first cut of what your project already calls its frozen benchmark:

45
00:02:56,116 --> 00:02:59,861
M1 第 8 版，留出非经典单核细胞
M1, version eight, holding out non-classical monocytes.

46
00:03:00,181 --> 00:03:02,220
它的规格文件是 m1_modern.yaml
Its spec is m1_modern.yaml,

47
00:03:02,220 --> 00:03:06,901
而 Josh 已经把其中的模型设置粘贴进了核心文件
and Josh already pasted its model settings into the core file,

48
00:03:06,901 --> 00:03:08,864
就在 scGenModel 上方不远处
a little above scGenModel.

49
00:03:09,033 --> 00:03:13,269
它的成绩表由 22_v08_results 这个 notebook 写出
Its scorecard, written by the notebook twenty-two v08 results,

50
00:03:13,269 --> 00:03:15,113
记录了要对上的数字
records the numbers to hit.

51
00:03:15,433 --> 00:03:19,422
identity 的均值 R² 是 0.554
The identity R squared of means is zero point five five four.

52
00:03:19,742 --> 00:03:24,815
它在 M1 第 8 版的每一行都一样，因为它描述的是数据本身
It's the same on every M1 version eight row, because it describes the data:

53
00:03:24,815 --> 00:03:28,062
原封不动的小鼠测试细胞，对比人类测试细胞
mouse test cells, unchanged, against human ones.

54
00:03:28,382 --> 00:03:31,006
这里不涉及训练，也不涉及抽样
No training and no sampling are involved,

55
00:03:31,006 --> 00:03:34,270
所以只要你的包读的是同一个文件、同一个切分
so once your package reads the same file and split,

56
00:03:34,270 --> 00:03:38,814
并且算的是均值 R²，就应该几乎能精确复现它
and computes R squared of means, it should reproduce it almost exactly.

57
00:03:39,134 --> 00:03:44,404
比较均值而不是逐个细胞，也顺带消除了第 313 行的崩溃
Comparing means, not cells, also removes the crash at line 313.

58
00:03:44,567 --> 00:03:49,879
然后是 scGen：0.927，来自 cellot 的自编码器
Then scGen: zero point nine two seven, from the cellot autoencoder,

59
00:03:49,879 --> 00:03:54,636
它的运行结果在集群上 cellot 的 results 文件夹里
whose run sits on the cluster under cellot's results folder.

60
00:03:54,956 --> 00:03:57,388
要对上这个数，适配器就得封装这个模型
To aim for it, your adapter wraps that model.

61
00:03:57,708 --> 00:04:01,402
这个数是对 80 个细胞的抽样取平均，要用同样的方法算
It averages eighty-cell samples, so compute it the same way,

62
00:04:01,402 --> 00:04:04,727
训练也会带来随机波动，所以在容差范围内对上即可
and since training adds noise, aim within a tolerance.

63
00:04:05,047 --> 00:04:07,580
另外，你不需要把 cellot 从头追一遍
And you don't need to trace all of cellot:

64
00:04:07,580 --> 00:04:11,319
只需打开适配器会调用的那几个函数，第四集讲过
open only the few calls your adapter makes, from episode four.

65
00:04:11,639 --> 00:04:13,439
你自己的成绩表就是检验
Your own scorecard is the check.

66
00:04:18,867 --> 00:04:20,481
SOLID 放在哪里？
Where does SOLID fit?

67
00:04:20,531 --> 00:04:23,429
把它当作代码开始难改、难测的时候用的指南针
Treat it as a compass for the moment something hurts,

68
00:04:23,429 --> 00:04:25,229
而不是第一天就要逐条打勾的清单
not a checklist for day one.

69
00:04:25,416 --> 00:04:27,955
每个字母都已经指向这个文件里的某个位置
Each letter already points at a spot in this file.

70
00:04:28,134 --> 00:04:31,919
单一职责：数据类只负责加载数据
Single responsibility: the data classes only load data,

71
00:04:31,919 --> 00:04:35,430
所以基因对齐和切分应该放在它们旁边
so gene alignment and splitting belong beside them.

72
00:04:35,750 --> 00:04:38,875
开闭原则：加入 CellOT 应该是新增一个类
Open-closed: adding CellOT should add a class,

73
00:04:38,875 --> 00:04:41,254
而不是去改 setup 里那一串 if
not edit the chain of ifs in setup.

74
00:04:41,574 --> 00:04:44,176
一个「名字到类」的字典就能做到
A dictionary from names to classes does that.

75
00:04:44,334 --> 00:04:48,409
里氏替换：每个模型都必须信守契约的承诺
Liskov substitution: every model must keep the contract's promise.

76
00:04:48,729 --> 00:04:50,569
契约里的 train 接收训练数据
The contract's train takes training data,

77
00:04:50,569 --> 00:04:52,803
而 IdentityModel 的 train 什么都不接收
but IdentityModel's takes none.

78
00:04:53,123 --> 00:04:59,395
第 133 行照着 IdentityModel 来写，于是信守契约的 scGen 反而出错了
Line 133 followed IdentityModel, so scGen, which keeps the contract, broke.

79
00:04:59,715 --> 00:05:03,811
Python 只检查名字、不检查参数，所以只有测试能抓到它
Python checks names, not inputs, so only a test can catch this.

80
00:05:03,967 --> 00:05:11,050
接口隔离：评估只需要一个方法，它的契约也只要求这一个
Interface segregation: an evaluation needs one method, and its contract asks for only one.

81
00:05:11,050 --> 00:05:18,528
依赖倒置：Experiment 只和契约打交道，从不导入 scgen 这个库
Dependency inversion: the Experiment talks to the contract. It never imports the scgen library;

82
00:05:18,528 --> 00:05:21,204
只有 scGenModel 在第 248 行导入它
only scGenModel does, at line 248.

83
00:05:21,367 --> 00:05:23,350
至于重构（不改变功能、只调整代码结构）
And refactoring,

84
00:05:23,350 --> 00:05:28,066
可以等到第三个模型出现时再做
meaning reshaping code without changing what it does, can wait until the third model arrives.

85
00:05:32,533 --> 00:05:37,951
所以每次坐下来都走这个循环：把你希望能跑通的调用写成一个小测试
So here's the loop for every session. Write the call you wish worked, as a small test.

86
00:05:37,951 --> 00:05:43,242
运行它；读它遇到的第一个错误，错误信息就在 traceback 的最后一行
Run it. Read the first error it hits: its message is the last line of the traceback.

87
00:05:43,400 --> 00:05:46,216
做最小的修改，让程序越过那一行
Make the smallest change that gets past that line.

88
00:05:46,536 --> 00:05:49,586
测试通过了就提交，然后拿起下一张卡片
When the test passes, commit, and pick up the next card.

89
00:05:49,733 --> 00:05:53,852
你的卡片，按顺序是：先走 identity 这条路
Your cards, in order. Walk identity's path first,

90
00:05:53,852 --> 00:05:58,980
因为它有精确答案：让 evaluate 返回一张表
because it has an exact answer: make evaluate return a table,

91
00:05:58,980 --> 00:06:07,133
切分 M1 文件；算均值 R²，直到 identity 得到 0.554
split the M1 file, and compute R squared of means until identity gives zero point five five four.

92
00:06:07,133 --> 00:06:09,150
然后沿着 scGen 的报错足迹
Then walk scGen's trail,

93
00:06:09,150 --> 00:06:15,034
第 253、133、288 行，一路走到接近 0.927
lines 253, 133 and 288, until it lands near zero point nine two seven.

94
00:06:15,200 --> 00:06:19,408
回顾一下：骨架已经能走，报错给出顺序
Recap. The skeleton already walks, the errors give the order,

95
00:06:19,408 --> 00:06:23,822
第一个黄金数字是 identity 的 0.554
the first golden number is identity's zero point five five four,

96
00:06:23,822 --> 00:06:26,443
SOLID 留到代码开始难改、难测的时候再用
and SOLID is for when something hurts.

97
00:06:26,443 --> 00:06:28,512
动起来，比完美的计划更重要
Momentum beats a perfect plan.
